From 34c28c8fe1b9bb9ef1ee7272f892be355fdff049 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel <kernel@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:14:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] ik2: a token's launches fused - IK2_K_LCN / LRR / LDN /
 LMD / LKV (default off, same bits on)

The resident path's one-token step (fast_token_launches), Inkling-2-Mini on HIP with the production env: ~711
launches a token (11 a windowed visit outside the loop, 15 a full one, 16 / 20 in the loop, +4 a later pass's
start) -> ~550 with every switch on (9 / 10 / 13 / 14).  Each fused launch runs the unfused kernels' code with their
block sizes; a vector a part needs whole is computed again in each block that needs it (no "last block" added).

- IK2_K_LCN: a visit's MoE output (moe_combine_conv) left pending and written by the next visit's input-norm launch
  (combine_res / combine_res_rms: one block of 512, attn_res_vec4's body over states read back with plain loads),
  with the block state's and the drafter tap's copies; the embedding's norm with layer 0's (emb_norm2); the loop's
  passes copy no stream (lp_pre = block nb_pre's state, the bank read where it is).  -65 launches a token.
- IK2_K_LRR: the MoE input's attn_res_rms with the router rows and route_pick (res_router; the norm again in each of
  E / 16 blocks, the picks by the last block as IK2_HIP_FUSE's).  -24.
- IK2_K_LDN: a looped visit's MoE residual with its message gate's dots (res_dots, 4 ranks a block of 512).  -24.
- IK2_K_LMD: a looped visit's attention input - the pending MoE output (again in each block, its conv history moved
  on in rms_multi_shift's launch), the residual, the three gates' dots - in one launch.  -24.
- IK2_K_LKV (load): a full layer's q | r | gate | k | v as one planar Q8_0 matrix (wqrg / wk / wv its rows), its
  products one mv_q8p_conv with MvAlt + the dynamic-tap convs; the two tap products one mv_f16_pair.  -24.

Refactors, the same code for the unfused kernels: attn_res_vec4_body, moe_combine_conv_ch, lg_dots_body,
rms_multi_row, rms_row / route_pick LDG flag; loop_gates / loop_gate_rms dots_done.
tests/ik2_kernels_test.cu: test_k_launches - each fused launch against the unfused calls, every output bit for bit.
