 src/ik2/ik2_main.cu       | 235 +++++++++++++++-----
 tests/ik2_kernels_test.cu | 236 ++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 864 insertions(+), 113 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/INKLING2.md b/docs/INKLING2.md
index b003bde0..7d53888e 100644
--- a/docs/INKLING2.md
+++ b/docs/INKLING2.md
@@ -484,6 +484,21 @@ time): mode A only by default - the resident path's expert kernels, so the same
 VRAM; lane parity (`IK2_LANE=1`) sums in other bits there and is a test option. Run on a Radeon 8065S (Ubuntu, ROCm
 7.1), also set as a 12 and a 16 GB card (`IK2_VRAM_GB`: on an APU the free figures are capped, no ballast).
 
+**Fewer launches a token** (`IK2_K_LCN`, `_LRR`, `_LDN`, `_LMD`, `_LKV`, each `=1` to turn on, off by default; the
+resident path's one-token steps, not the offload path or two GPUs). A token's launches each cost ~2 us of gap on an
+RX 7900 XTX whatever they do, and Inkling-2-Mini's 48 visits took ~711 of them (11 a windowed visit outside the loop,
+16-21 inside it). Each switch merges small kernels into one launch whose blocks run the unfused kernels' code with
+their block sizes, so every value is the unfused launches' to the bit (`tests/ik2_kernels_test.cu`: each against
+them); a vector a part needs whole is computed again in each block that needs it (a few KB from L2), not left to "the
+last block" (which broke even on gfx1100). `LCN`: a visit's MoE output (combine + short conv + stream) is written by the
+next visit's input-norm launch, with the block state's and the drafter's tap's copies, and the loop's passes copy no
+stream (the core's input is block `nb_pre`'s state; the bank is read where it is): -65 launches a token. `LRR`: the MoE
+input's norm with the router (-24). `LDN`: a looped visit's MoE residual with its message gate's dots (-24). `LMD`: a
+looped visit's attention input - the pending MoE output, the residual, the three gates' dots - in one launch, the
+conv's history moved on in the norms' launch after (-24). `LKV` (at load): a full layer's q | r | gate | k | v as one
+planar Q8_0 matrix, its products one launch, the dynamic taps' two products one (-24). All on: ~550 launches a token
+(-161), 9 a windowed visit outside the loop, 13 inside it.
+
 **Defaults.** Thinking Machines' `generation_config.json`: temperature 1.0 (no top_p, no top_k: 1.0 and off).
 Thinking is the template's `reasoning_effort`, a name or a number in [0.0, 0.99]: `none` 0.0, `minimal` 0.1, `low`
 0.2, `medium` 0.7, `high` 0.9 (the template's default), `xhigh` and `max` 0.99.
